+# Language coverage diffs
+
+`diff_language_coverage` compares two versioned clinical language-pack coverage
+manifests and reports which locales were added, removed, improved, regressed,
+or otherwise changed. Release review can use it to spot language capability
+regressions without loading models, fixtures, or evaluation data. The module
+uses only the standard library and runs fully offline.
+
+```python
+from openmed.core.language_coverage_diff import diff_language_coverage
+
+digest = "sha256:" + "a" * 64
+before = {
+    "version": "3.2.0",
+    "entries": [
+        {
+            "locale": "hi",
+            "script": "Deva",
+            "identifier_classes": ["aadhaar"],
+            "surrogate_support": "partial",
+            "evidence_digest": digest,
+        },
+        {
+            "locale": "pt-BR",
+            "script": "Latn",
+            "identifier_classes": ["cpf", "phone"],
+            "surrogate_support": "full",
+            "evidence_digest": digest,
+        },
+    ],
+}
+after = {
+    "version": "3.3.0",
+    "entries": [
+        {
+            "locale": "pt-BR",
+            "script": "Latn",
+            "identifier_classes": ["cpf"],
+            "surrogate_support": "full",
+            "evidence_digest": digest,
+        },
+        {
+            "locale": "hi",
+            "script": "Deva",
+            "identifier_classes": ["aadhaar", "pan"],
+            "surrogate_support": "full",
+            "evidence_digest": digest,
+        },
+    ],
+}
+
+diff = diff_language_coverage(before, after)
+assert [(entry.locale, entry.status) for entry in diff.entries] == [
+    ("hi", "improved"),
+    ("pt-BR", "regressed"),
+]
+assert diff.has_regressions
+print(diff.to_markdown())
+```
+
+## Manifest format
+
+A manifest is a JSON-compatible mapping with exactly two keys:
+
+| Key | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `version` | Release label: 1-64 ASCII letters, digits, `.`, `+`, `_` or `-`. |
+| `entries` | List of per-locale coverage entries. |
+
+Each entry has exactly these keys:
+
+| Key | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `locale` | Locale tag, normalized with [`normalize_locale_tag`](locale-tags.md). |
+| `script` | Four-letter ISO 15924 script code, normalized to title case. |
+| `identifier_classes` | List of lowercase identifier class tokens such as `cpf` or `phone`. |
+| `surrogate_support` | One of `none`, `partial`, or `full`. |
+| `evidence_digest` | `sha256:` followed by 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters. |
+
+Unknown keys are rejected, so a manifest cannot carry fixture text, model
+paths, or raw evaluation examples into the diff output. Two entries that
+resolve to the same canonical locale, including through case variants or
+explicit aliases, are rejected as duplicates.
+
+## Statuses
+
+Locales are compared by canonical locale. Entry order and identifier-class
+order never affect the result, so reordered manifests produce byte-identical
+output.
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `added` | The locale exists only in the later manifest. |
+| `removed` | The locale exists only in the earlier manifest. |
+| `regressed` | An identifier class was dropped or surrogate support decreased. |
+| `improved` | Only new identifier classes or stronger surrogate support. |
+| `changed` | Only the script or evidence digest differs. |
+
+Regressions take precedence: a locale that gains one identifier class but loses
+another, or gains a class while surrogate support drops, is `regressed`.
+Locales that are identical in both manifests are listed under `unchanged` and
+counted, but they get no diff entry. `has_regressions` is true when any locale
+was removed or regressed.
+
+## Output
+
+`to_json()` renders indented JSON with sorted keys and a trailing newline.
+`to_markdown()` renders a summary count table followed by one row per changed
+locale. Both are byte-stable for the same inputs. The Markdown output
+says only that an evidence digest changed; the JSON output contains the before
+and after digests.
+
+Explicit locale aliases use the same rules as the locale tag helpers:
+
+```python
+diff = diff_language_coverage(before, after, aliases={"pt_BR": "pt-BR"})
+```
+
+## Failures and privacy
+
+Malformed manifests raise `LanguageCoverageDiffError`, a `ValueError` whose
+`.category` and string are the same constant, such as
+`coverage_manifest_keys_invalid`, `coverage_locale_invalid`,
+`coverage_locale_duplicate`, or `coverage_evidence_digest_invalid`. Rejected
+values are never embedded in the error.
+
+The diff does not run evaluation, decide release gates, or measure translation
+quality. It only compares caller-supplied coverage metadata.
+
+## Verification
+
+```bash
+uv run --frozen --extra dev pytest tests/unit/core/test_language_coverage_diff.py -q
+```
+
+The tests cover equal, added, removed, changed, alias, and reordered manifests
+with golden JSON and Markdown output, plus value-free validation failures. No
+model weights or network calls are needed.
